@startuml sd09_closures_switch_commands
!include ../style.iuml
autonumber

actor Dispatcher as D
participant "CTC Office" as CTC
participant "Central\nHarness" as H
participant "HwTrackController\n(on the Pi)" as Ctrl
participant "Wayside" as W
participant "Track Controller\nwindow" as Win

D -> CTC : close a block; in maintenance\nmode, set switch Red:15 reverse
CTC -> H : outputs: closed blocks (full set),\nswitch commands (maintenance only)
H -> Ctrl : STEP: ctc.closed_blocks,\nctc.switch_commands
Ctrl -> Ctrl : validate keys (BlockRef)\nand positions
Ctrl -> W : scan(...)
W -> W : CLOSED_n = 1 for each\nclosed block it governs
W -> W : CTCSW_15 = 1 (a command is in effect)\nCTCREV_15 = 1 (it is reverse)
note right of W
  No maintenance flag: a switch command
  in effect is maintenance mode.
end note
W -> W : record closures and requests\nin the snapshot
W --> Win : (next view) "CTC asks: reverse";\nmaintenance banner lists closures\nand commands
@enduml
